RP1 ADC Linux Driver
 - Intended for learning purposes and as a project of interest.

Description:

Linux kernel driver for interaction with the ADC peripheral on the RP1 IO controller.

The creation of this driver was primarily for learning purposes to explore low-level MMIO-based perihperal access, including physical-to-virtual memory mapping with ioremap(), register access using readl(), and interaction with RP1 peripheral register blocks from kernel space.

Generally speaking, this is developed as a learning project to gather experience with Linux kernel development, and hardware register interfacing.
